<!--
  reBot B601-RS assets, defaults, actuators and gripper coupling; the body tree
  is rebot_arm.xml. Meshes are the base package's own STL files, resolved
  through package:// URIs, not copies. MuJoCo cannot load the base package's
  COLLADA visuals (printed trim, wrist bracket, D435), so assets/ holds them
  converted to STL in the same frame and units, one file per embedded
  material; see assets/NOTICE.md.

  ros2_control takes its interfaces from the actuators: one position actuator
  per URDF motor joint, named after the joint. Gains are the real driver's
  motion-mode kp/kd (rebot.urdf.xacro), forces its effort limits. The links
  are gravity-compensated (gravcomp in rebot_arm.xml), unlike the real arm in
  motion mode: sagging out of the folded rest pose puts link2 and link5 in
  collision, and MoveIt then refuses to plan from it.
-->
<mujocoinclude>
